# _redirects — New Barbershop (Cloudflare Pages syntax)
# ============================================================================
# LAUNCH CASE THIS FILE IS WRITTEN FOR: OLD DOMAIN (newbarbershop1.com).
# Drop this file at the root of the Astro build output (public/_redirects)
# when the new site launches on newbarbershop1.com. All rules are 301.
# Source map: seo-tracking-plan.md §2.2 (Agent D, 2026-11-15), reconciled
# against Search Console's Pages report before launch (plan §2.2 step) —
# any indexed URL not listed here gets a rule added BEFORE DNS flips.
#
# NEW-DOMAIN VARIANT (launch on newbarbershoporlando.com instead):
# Keep this file as-is — the rules still fire for anyone who reaches the
# NEW domain with a legacy path (typed, shared, or printed links).
# What this file CANNOT do: redirect traffic on the OLD domain. Without
# control of the old domain's DNS/hosting there is no redirect surface
# there at all; old-domain URLs only survive if the ownership push or
# transfer lands, in which case deploy this same file (or a domain-level
# forward) on the old domain pointing at the new one. See
# new-domain-memo.md play M1.
#
# HOSTNAME RULES ARE NOT HERE ON PURPOSE: Cloudflare Pages _redirects
# matches paths on one hostname only. www -> apex (canonical) is a
# Cloudflare Redirect Rule / Bulk Redirect at the zone level (Agent E,
# cutover runbook) — canonical host: https://newbarbershop1.com.
#
# Format: <from> <to> 301 — both slash and no-slash variants are listed
# for legacy paths so matching never depends on trailing-slash handling.
# ============================================================================

